# SonoJS registry dependencies

When adding or porting a registry component / block / chart, **dependencies must be complete in the registry JSON**. Users discover them from **`sonojs add` output** (`+` lines), not from a docs “Dependencies / npm i …” code block.

## Declare in `scripts/registry-items.mjs`

| Field | Use for |
|---|---|
| `registryDependencies` | Other SonoJS registry items the source imports (`separator`, `button`, `spinner`, …). CLI installs them first and prints each as `+ path`. |
| `dependencies` | npm packages the installed file needs (`react-day-picker`, `date-fns`, `recharts`, …). CLI prints each as `+ <pkg>` then `npm i …`. |

Do **not** omit a dep because “the monorepo already has it” — consumers only get what the registry JSON lists.

**Pin versions when latest would break the component.** Example: calendar needs DayPicker v9 APIs — declare `react-day-picker@^9.14.0`, not bare `react-day-picker` (npm would pull v10 and drop dropdown border/radius). Versioned specs are always passed to `npm i` so a wrong major already in the consumer gets corrected.

After edits: `npm run registry:build` and confirm `public/r/<name>.json`.

## Examples / demos

If a **docs example** imports another installable SonoJS component that the main item’s source also needs, add it to `registryDependencies`.

If it is example-only chrome, keep it out of the item’s registry deps — still fine for the docs preview.

## Docs Installation + “Also needs”

Use shared `DocsInstallation` on every component docs page. Same visual language as button-group example footers (“This example also needs …”).

```tsx
<DocsInstallation name="calendar" />
```

Renders:

1. Code player — only `npx @sonojs/ui@latest add <name>`
2. Soft bar under it when the item has deps — **Also needs** `npx … add button && npm i date-fns lucide-react react-day-picker` (command only; no duplicate name list)

- `registryDependencies` → `npx @sonojs/ui@latest add …`
- npm `dependencies` → `npm i …` for notable packages (**include** `lucide-react`, `react-day-picker`, `date-fns`, …)
- Skip only baseline noise: `clsx`, `tailwind-merge`, `radix-ui`, `class-variance-authority`
- **Do not** invent a second section titled “Dependencies”
- button-group → Also needs `separator`; calendar → Also needs `button`, `date-fns`, `lucide-react`, `react-day-picker@^9.14.0`

### Example footers

Per-variant extras (not pulled by the main item) use the same bar via `requires` / `npmRequires` on `VariantExample`:

```ts
requires: ["card", "field", "input-group"],
npmRequires: ["lucide-react"],
```

Label stays **This example also needs**.

## CLI contract (required everywhere)

`sonojs add <name>` must:

1. Recursively install `registryDependencies` (each file logged with `+`).
2. Collect `dependencies`, skip init baseline (`clsx`, `tailwind-merge`) and bare names already in the consumer `package.json`, then **run `npm i …` for the rest** (log each as `+ <pkg>`). Version-pinned specs (e.g. `react-day-picker@^9.14.0`) always install so the range is enforced. Do not only print a tip — missing packages cause TS2307.

Shared helper: `packages/cli/src/install-npm.mjs` and `packages/ui/cli/src/install-npm.mjs` (keep in sync).

Example after `add calendar`:

```text
  + components/ui/button.tsx
  + components/ui/calendar.tsx

Installing npm packages:
  + date-fns
  + lucide-react
  + react-day-picker@^9.14.0
  (npm i runs here)
```

## Checklist (new / updated item)

- [ ] `registryDependencies` lists every SonoJS UI import in the component source
- [ ] `dependencies` lists every required npm package
- [ ] Docs page uses `<DocsInstallation name="…" />` only (no npm Dependencies block)
- [ ] `npm run registry:build` run
- [ ] Spot-check: `add` copies files with `+` and actually runs `npm i` for missing packages (no TS2307)
